  "body": "From the review of PR #205 (#202): since #140 marches sideways rapids, the march subsumes `hidden_along` for a flat tool on a straight lateral rapid, so deleting the `hidden_along` call in `verify/rapids.rs` would leave every overhang_laws test green.\n\nDone means: a fixture the march can't see but the hidden-stock law does - e.g. a ball or bull tip near the rim under a ledge, where the tip lift lets the column read pass - pins the rapid arm (convicted with the call, clean without it).",
